			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50328896\"><span>Ask HN: Which TV do you recommend for privacy?</span></a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50328896\">687 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=LecroJS\"><span>LecroJS</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50328896\">1 day ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50328896\">831 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>I haven’t owned a TV in years and would like one that respects my privacy. Are there any TV’s which do this well? I am looking for something in the 60”to 80”range and would like a 4k display with at least 60hz display. I don’t mind paying a premium.<p>I have heard good things about Apple TV as a better alternative to most smart TV native apps. Would some TV’s pair better with this than others for privacy? I don’t want the TV doing anything other than being the display for Apple TV.</p><p>I am curious what success others have had.</p></span></div></div></div></div>",
